The device runtime's barrier across the teams of a cooperative kernel,
merk_device_grid_barrier (docs/INPROGRESS.md, GPU processes that run loops,
(c)): a kernel linked as a GPU process's image is, launched cooperatively
through liboffload with as many teams as can be resident at once, checks in
each round that every thread sees the other teams' writes of that round. The
queues are limited to half the GPU's compute units, so that a GPU that drives
a display keeps the rest.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: clang++ --target=amdgcn-amd-amdhsa -mcpu=%offload-arch -flto -O2 -c %S/Inputs/grid-barrier-kernel.cpp -o %t.o
RUN: clang --target=amdgcn-amd-amdhsa -mcpu=%offload-arch -flto -O2 %t.o %merk-lib-dir/merk-process-start-amdgcn.o %merk-lib-dir/libmerkdevice-amdgcn.a -lc -lm -o %t.elf
RUN: clang++ -O2 -std=c++17 %S/Inputs/grid-barrier-host.cpp %libomp-flags -lLLVMOffload -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env LIBOMPTARGET_AMDGPU_CU_MASK=0-39 %t %t.elf 64 1000 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=T64
RUN: %libomp-env LIBOMPTARGET_AMDGPU_CU_MASK=0-39 %t %t.elf 256 1000 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=T256
RUN: %libomp-env LIBOMPTARGET_AMDGPU_CU_MASK=0-39 %t %t.elf 1024 1000 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=T1024
T64: 64 threads, 1000 rounds: 0 wrong
T256: 256 threads, 1000 rounds: 0 wrong
T1024: 1024 threads, 1000 rounds: 0 wrong
